                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "You can view my review & gameplay here: https://youtu.be/B1C-R7SeXNg\n\n[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers[/h1]\n\nThis game is now completely free to play. It was a paid game in Early Access, so you could see some of the issues it had when you play it. However, it's still a fun game to play as long as you're okay with the limitations of the game. Currently, there are only 7 songs total and 3 different environments to play in. There are no difficulty levels. There are basically no options in the game.\n\nThe game consists of playing virtual drumsticks on either drum pads and/or piano keys. The drum pads & piano keys will vary depending on the song. You basically hit them to the beat of the music for the most part (although they don't always coincide with each other).\n\nUnfortunately, the crowd noise is pretty loud as far as either applause or boos. So you may want to prefer the simple environment of the Black Lounge where at least you can just hear the music. The instruments actually do make noise, except for the upper drum pads which are silent. However, your score does get marked off for that. There are leaderboards, both local and online. I enjoyed the soundtrack, but it is all electronic dance music so if you're not into that then you may not enjoy it as much.\n\nThere are also some issues with the game. I did notice some hit detection issues, some random lag spikes, & the music cutting off for no apparent reason during gameplay. Despite those issues, I had fun playing this game. It's not the best music rhythm game out there, but it's definitely the best free one out there with its own music (with McOSU you have to bring your own music).\n\n[b]Rate 7/10.[/b]",
